.TH PHASECTL 1 "August 2026" "phasectl 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phasectl \- cognitive-mode manager for engineering sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phasectl
[\fB--model\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--backend\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--api-base\fR \fIURL\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phasectl
runs a sequence of LLM API calls under a named
.I phase
\(em orient, ideate, design, impl, validate, snapshot \(em each with its own
system prompt, temperature, and token budget. Turns are persisted to a local
SQLite database; when a session is closed, it is compressed into a
summary and linked in a JSON-backed graph. Symbol lookup for the impl and
validate phases is delegated to an external MCP-speaking indexer over stdio.
The LLM backend (anthropic, openai, ollama, openrouter, or a custom
OpenAI-compatible endpoint) is chosen in
.IR config.toml ,
overridable per invocation with
.BR --model ,
.BR --backend ,
and
.BR --api-base .
.PP
The bundled phase prompts describe
.I posture,
not domain knowledge. Any project-specific content belongs in a per-user
override at
.IR ~/.config/phasectl/phases/<name>.toml .
.PP
.B phasectl
is read-only against the user's codebase: it reads git state, indexed
symbols, and transcripts, and writes only under
.IR ~/.config/phasectl/ .
No command creates, modifies, or deletes files under the project path.
.PP
.B phasectl
runs entirely in userspace: no root, no system services, no open ports, no
background processes. The only network traffic is outbound HTTPS to the
configured LLM endpoint (or localhost for Ollama). Credentials are kept in
the system keychain or a chmod-600 file. No telemetry. Licensed under MIT.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS start
.B phasectl start
[\fB--project\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--phase\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--seed\fR \fIPATH\fR]...
[\fB--no-fuse\fR]
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
Open a new session for a project.
Exits 1 if a session is already active or if the phase name is unknown.
In the default
.B orient
phase (unless
.BR --no-fuse ),
phasectl fuses git state of the indexed repo, the closed summary of the last
session, and the tail of the most recent external coding-agent transcript for
that repo (e.g. Claude Code sessions under
.IR ~/.claude/projects/ )
into a
.B "Resume here:"
block on stdout. Each
.B --seed
file (\fB.md\fR, \fB.txt\fR, or \fB.json\fR, max 200 KB) is compressed by the
LLM and injected as system context; the flag repeats.
.SS chat
.B phasectl chat
\fIMESSAGE\fR
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
Send a message under the current phase's system prompt.
When the running token estimate exceeds the phase budget, older turns are
compressed into a summary before the request. In the
.B impl
and
.B validate
phases the model may call whatever tools the configured MCP server exposes
via
.BR tools/list ;
the tool loop runs until the model produces a plain-text reply.
.SS switch
.B phasectl switch --phase
\fINAME\fR
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
Change the active session's phase. Subsequent
.B chat
calls use the new phase's prompt, temperature, budget, and tool set. Prior
turns remain visible.
.SS close
.B phasectl close
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
Close the active session and produce a snapshot summary.
Uncompressed turns are handed to the
.B snapshot
phase prompt via the compression model. The result is stored on the session
row, and any
.B RFC-<n>
or
.B DECISION-<n>
tokens found in it are linked into
.IR ~/.config/phasectl/graph.json .
Prints
.RI < session-id >
.RI < turns >\(->1
.RI < tokens >t
on stdout.
.SS status
.B phasectl status
[\fB--json\fR]
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
Show whether a session is active for the default project. With an active
session, prints its short id, phase, token estimate, and turn count. With
none, prints the date and short id of the most recent closed session. With
.B --json
emits an object with
.BR session_id ,
.BR project ,
.BR phase ,
.BR tokens ,
.BR turns ,
and (when no session is active)
.BR last_session .
.SS index
.B phasectl index
[\fB--project\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--path\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB--register-only\fR]
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
Resolve the indexer binary from
.RI [tools].mcp_command
(first token, e.g.
.B jcodemunch-mcp
from
.RB \(oq "jcodemunch-mcp serve" \(cq)
and invoke
.RI \(oq< binary "> index <" abs_path >\(cq
as a subprocess. The resolved absolute path is stored at
.RI [projects. <name> ].index_path
in
.IR config.toml ,
so later runs can be spelled just
.B phasectl index --project
.IR NAME
to re-index the stored path. First-time indexing requires
.BR --path .
.PP
.B --register-only
stores the path in config without invoking any indexer, for MCP servers
that handle indexing externally. If the configured binary has no
.B index
subcommand, phasectl prints a hint to run
.B --register-only
instead.
.PP
Exit 1 on missing path, missing binary, or indexer error.
.SS query
.B phasectl query
\fISYMBOL\fR
[\fB--project\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--json\fR]
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
Search the indexed symbols of a project. Standalone \(em no session needed.
Requires a prior
.BR "phasectl index" .
Exit 4 if the project has no stored index or the indexer reports an error.
.SS graph
.B phasectl graph
[\fB--project\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--json\fR]
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
Show closed sessions with their linked RFCs and DECISIONs from
.IR ~/.config/phasectl/graph.json .
Standalone. Emits an empty result when nothing has been closed yet.
.SS loose
.B phasectl loose
[\fB--project\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--path\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB--base\fR \fIBRANCH\fR]
[\fB--json\fR]
[\fB--synthesize\fR]
[\fB--quiet\fR]
.PP
List every loose thread in a git repo: uncommitted files, unmerged branches,
stashes, unpushed commits, and extra worktrees. Standalone. Works on any git
repo via
.BR --path ;
otherwise reads the project's stored
.BR index_path .
.B --base
defaults to
.BR main ,
falling back to
.B master
or
.B origin/HEAD .
.B --synthesize
adds one LLM-produced
.B "Most stale:"
top line (requires the API key); all other output is offline.
.SS check
.B phasectl check
[\fB--project\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB--json\fR]
.PP
Smoke-test every subsystem: config, auth, db, phases, index, mcp, git.
No LLM calls; no API key required. Each row is one of:
.B \(oq\(cq
(configured and working),
.B \(oq\(em\(cq
(not configured yet \(em a setup step the user hasn't taken, e.g. no API
key with a key-requiring backend, or no stored index path for the
project), or
.B \(oq\(dg\(cq
(broken \(em a configured subsystem that failed, e.g. a corrupt DB or an
unreachable MCP server). Exit 0 unless any row is broken.
.SS auth set
.B phasectl auth set
.PP
Read an LLM API key from a hidden prompt and store it (macOS Keychain,
freedesktop secret-service, or
.I ~/.config/phasectl/credentials
chmod 600, in that preference order). Consulted only when
.B $PHASECTL_API_KEY
and
.B $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
are unset.
.SS auth status
.B phasectl auth status
.PP
Report which source phasectl would load the key from. Prints one of
.RB \(oq "key: from environment" \(cq,
.RB \(oq "key: configured (credentials file)" \(cq,
or
.RB \(oq "key: not set" \(cq.
Does not validate the key against the API.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration lives under
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/phasectl ,
defaulting to
.BR ~/.config/phasectl .
The file
.B config.toml
is created on first run and read by every command.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[provider]
# backend: anthropic | openai | ollama | openrouter | custom
backend = "anthropic"

# leave empty to let the backend pick its own sensible default
#   anthropic:  claude-sonnet-4-6, claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
#   openai:     gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini
#   ollama:     llama3.1:70b, llama3.1:8b
#   openrouter: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6, openai/gpt-4o
model             = ""
compression_model = ""

# leave empty for provider defaults, or set for custom endpoints
api_base = ""

[storage]
db_path = ""            # empty = ~/.config/phasectl/sessions.db

[graph]
path = ""               # empty = ~/.config/phasectl/graph.json

# Optional. When a command omits --project, phasectl uses defaults.project
# if set; otherwise it infers the project from cwd (longest matching
# [projects.*].index_path, then the enclosing git repo's basename).
# [defaults]
# project = "myproject"

[claude_code]
projects_dir = ""       # override the auto-detected coding-agent transcript dir

[tools]
mcp_command = "jcodemunch-mcp serve"   # spawned for indexing and code-lookup tools

[projects.myproject]
index_path = "/abs/path/to/myproject"   # written by 'phasectl index'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Provider values can be overridden per invocation with
.BR --model ,
.BR --backend ,
and
.BR --api-base
on the outer
.B phasectl
call, or with
.B --model
on
.BR chat .
.SH PHASES
The bundled phases live in the package and can be inspected via
.BR "phasectl check" .
A file placed at
.BI ~/.config/phasectl/phases/ NAME .toml
takes precedence over the bundled prompt of the same name; user names not in
the bundled set are available as new phases.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[phase]
name         = "impl"
temperature  = 0.1
token_budget = 10000
tools_allowed = []

system_prompt = """
You are in impl mode: ...
"""
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/phasectl/config.toml
Global settings.
.TP
.B ~/.config/phasectl/credentials
LLM API key, plain text, chmod 600. Read only when neither
.B $PHASECTL_API_KEY
nor
.B $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
is set, and only when the system keychain doesn't have the key.
.TP
.B ~/.config/phasectl/sessions.db
SQLite database with
.B sessions
and
.B turns
tables.
.TP
.B ~/.config/phasectl/graph.json
NetworkX MultiDiGraph on disk (node_link_data format). Contains nodes for
sessions, RFCs, decisions, and (in future) symbols.
.TP
.B ~/.config/phasectl/phases/
Optional per-user phase overrides. Each file replaces the bundled phase of
the same name.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PHASECTL_API_KEY
LLM API key. When set, wins over
.B $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
and every stored source.
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
LLM API key. Consulted when
.B $PHASECTL_API_KEY
is unset. Wins over stored sources.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the phasectl config tree. Defaults to
.BR ~/.config .
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Consulted when
.B start
looks for coding-agent transcripts to fuse (functional dependency on
Claude Code's on-disk layout). Defaults to
.BR ~/.claude .
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
User error: bad flag, missing path, session-already-active on
.BR start ,
missing API key, phase not found, failed
.BR check ,
graph query failed, loose repo missing.
.TP
.B 2
API failure: compression or chat error, invalid API key.
.TP
.B 3
No active session for
.BR chat ,
.BR switch ,
or
.BR close .
.TP
.B 4
Query index unavailable or indexer error in
.BR query .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
First-time setup for a new project:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
phasectl auth set
phasectl index --project my-api --path .
phasectl check --project my-api
.fi
.RE
.PP
A typical work session:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
phasectl start  --project my-api --phase orient
phasectl chat   "where are we?"
phasectl switch --phase design
phasectl chat   "we need a retry policy for the outbound webhook"
phasectl switch --phase impl
phasectl chat   "implement the design"
phasectl close
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspecting the repo without spending a turn:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
phasectl loose  --project my-api
phasectl query  RetryPolicy --project my-api --json
phasectl graph  --project my-api --json | jq .
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1),
.BR jq (1)
.PP
Project sources and additional design notes:
.BR https://github.com/praveenprk/phasectl .
